<title>UK: SOCCER-KENNY DALGLISH'S CAREER FACTFILE.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-KENNY DALGLISH'S CAREER FACTFILE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Factfile on the career of Kenny</p>
<p>Dalglish:</p>
<p>1951: Born Glasgow, March 4</p>
<p>1966: Scottish schoolboy international</p>
<p>1967: Joined Glasgow Celtic as apprentice</p>
<p>1968: Signed as professional by Celtic</p>
<p>1971: Scotland debut as substitute v Belgium</p>
<p>1972: Scored first goal for Scotland v Denmark (won 2-0)</p>
<p>1977: Joined Liverpool for 440,000 pounds ($732,000)</p>
<p>1979: English Footballer of the Year</p>
<p>1983: English Footballer of the Year and Player's Player of</p>
<p>Year</p>
<p>1984: Scored record-equalling 30th and last Scotland goal v</p>
<p>Spain (won 3-1)</p>
<p>1985: Appointed Liverpool player-manager</p>
<p>1986: Made record 102nd and final appearance for Scotland (v</p>
<p>Luxembourg)</p>
<p>1991: (Feb) Resigned as Liverpool player-manager</p>
<p>1991: (Oct) Appointed Blackburn Rovers manager</p>
<p>1995: Resigned as Blackburn manager, appointed Director of</p>
<p>Football</p>
<p>1996: (Aug) Quits as Blackburn's Director of Football by</p>
<p>mutual consent</p>
<p>1996: (Dec) Appointed as scout at Glasgow Rangers</p>
<p>1997: Appointed as Kevin Keegan's successor as manager of</p>
<p>Newcastle United</p>
<p>- - -</p>
<p>Honours (as player and player-manager)</p>
<p>European Champions Cup winner: 1978, 1981, 1984. Runner-up 1985</p>
<p>European Super Cup winner: 1977</p>
<p>Scottish League Championship medals: 1971-72, 1972-73, 1973-74,</p>
<p>1976-77</p>
<p>Scottish F.A. Cup winner: 1972, 1974, 1975, 1977</p>
<p>Scottish League Cup winner: 1975</p>
<p>English League Championship medals: 1978-79, 1979-80, 1981-82,</p>
<p>1982-83, 1983-84, 1985-86 (player-manager), 1988</p>
<p>(player-manager), 1990 (player-manager)</p>
<p>English F.A. Cup winner: 1986, 1989 (player-manager)</p>
<p>English League Cup winner: 1981, 1982, 1983, 1984</p>
<p>English Footballer of the Year: 1978-79, 1982-83</p>
<p>Scotland: Schoolboy, youth, and Under-23 international, record</p>
<p>102 senior caps, 30 goals (record shared with Denis Law)</p>
<p>- - -</p>
<p>Honours (as manager only)</p>
<p>English League championship winner: Blackburn 1995</p>
<p>English second division promotion: Blackburn 1992</p>
</text>
